#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186228891 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "eb295d6c-62fe-59bc-a139-49785ac98f1f" :knowledge-point/title "Using Linearity of Fourier Series"}] :question/id #uuid "cf8f2367-68af-5ef4-ac2e-5a73e37695d9" :question/math-academy-id "e-21803" :question/problem "$\\begin{bmatrix}f(x) & ∼\\frac{a_{0}}{2} + ∑_(n = 1)^(∞)a_{n}\\cos (nx) + b_{n}\\sin (nx) \\\\ g(x) & ∼\\frac{c_{0}}{2} + ∑_(n = 1)^(∞)c_{n}\\cos (nx) + d_{n}\\sin (nx)\\end{bmatrix}$\n\nLet $f(x)$ and $g(x)$ be $2\\pi$-periodic extensions of some functions from $[MATH: x \\in [-\\pi,\\pi)]$ to $x \\in \\mathbb{R}$ with the Fourier series shown above. What are the Fourier constant coefficient, the $3\\textrm{rd}$ Fourier sine coefficient, and the $8\\textrm{th}$ Fourier cosine coefficient of $-3f(x)+4g(x)$?" :question/worked-solution "Let $f(x)$ and $g(x)$ be $2\\pi$-periodic functions with Fourier series\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}f(x) & ∼\\frac{a_{0}}{2} + ∑_(n = 1)^(∞)(a_{n}\\cos (nx) + b_{n}\\sin (nx)), \\\\ g(x) & ∼\\frac{c_{0}}{2} + ∑_(n = 1)^(∞)(c_{n}\\cos (nx) + d_{n}\\sin (nx))\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nThen for any constants $\\alpha$ and $\\beta$,\n\n$$\n\\alpha f(x) + \\beta g(x) \\sim \\frac{\\alpha a_0 + \\beta c_0}{2} + \\sum_{n=1}^{\\infty} \\Big((\\alpha a_n + \\beta c_n)\\cos(nx) + (\\alpha b_n + \\beta d_n)\\sin(nx) \\Big)\n$$\n\nUsing the linearity property of Fourier series, the corresponding Fourier coefficients of $-3f(x)+4g(x)$ are\n\n- $-3a_0+4c_0$ for the constant coefficient,\n- $-3a_n+4c_n$, $n \\ge 1$ for the cosine coefficients, and\n- $-3b_n+4d_n$, $n \\ge 1$ for the sine coefficients.\n\nTherefore,\n\n- the Fourier constant coefficient of $-3f(x)+4g(x)$ is $-3a_0+4c_0$,\n- the $3$rd Fourier sine coefficient of $-3f(x)+4g(x)$ is $-3b_3+4d_3$, and\n- the $8$th Fourier cosine coefficient of $-3f(x)+4g(x)$ is $-3a_8+4c_8$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186228892 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "532a73e6-e026-57c9-9bad-57cd2f75b6df" :knowledge-point/title "Parity Recognition and Series Type"}] :question/id #uuid "f43f5028-9314-5123-bbd8-85dc5c4a9b2b" :question/math-academy-id "e-21804" :question/problem "Consider the function $f(x)=x\\cos(2x)$ on $x \\in [-\\pi,\\pi]$. Complete the statements below by filling in the blanks.\nDetermine if the function $f(x)$ is odd or even, and which terms of the corresponding Fourier series of $f(x)$ must be zero." :question/worked-solution "To determine whether $f$ is even or odd, we compare $f(-x)$ and $f(x){:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf(-x) &= (-x)\\cos (2(-x)) \\\\\n&= (-x)\\cos (-2x) \\\\\n&= (-x)\\cos (2x) \\\\\n&=-f(x)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince\n\n$$\nf(-x) = -f(x)\n$$\n\nwe have that $f$ is odd.\n\nFor Fourier series on $[-\\pi,\\pi]$, the cosine coefficients are given by\n\n$$\na_n=\\frac{1}{\\pi}\\int_{-\\pi}^{\\pi} f(x)\\cos(nx)\\,\\text{d}x\n$$\n\nand the constant coefficient is\n\n$$\na_0=\\frac{1}{\\pi}\\int_{-\\pi}^{\\pi} f(x)\\,\\text{d}x\n$$\n\nHere, $f(x)$ is odd and $\\cos(nx)$ is even, so $f(x)\\cos(nx)$ is odd. Also, $f(x)$ itself is odd.\n\nNow, the integral of an odd function over $[-\\pi,\\pi]$ is $0$. Thus, $a_n=0$ for all\n\n$$\nn\\ge1\n$$\n\nand $a_0=0$.\n\nTherefore, the function $f(x)$ is $\\bbox[4pt, border: solid 1pt gainsboro]{\\text{odd}}$ and the $\\bbox[4pt, border: solid 1pt gainsboro]{\\text{cosine}}$ terms in its Fourier series must be zero."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186228893 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f30ca427-3074-56c3-828a-1327d7b172b0" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Effects of Vertical Shifting and Horizontal Reflection on Coefficients"}] :question/id #uuid "848cc0af-b940-5ead-81ac-49cc6d2f4989" :question/math-academy-id "e-21805" :question/problem "$f(x) \\sim \\dfrac{a_0}{2}+\\sum_{n=1}^{\\infty}a_n\\cos(nx)+b_n\\sin(nx)$\nLet $f(x)$ be the $2\\pi$-periodic extesion of a function from $[MATH: x \\in [-\\pi,\\pi)]$ to $x \\in \\mathbb{R}$ with the Fourier series shown above. What is the $5$th sine Fourier coefficient of $f(-x)$?" :question/worked-solution "The Fourier series of $f(x)$ is\n\n$$\nf(x) \\sim \\dfrac{a_0}{2}+\\sum_{n=1}^{\\infty}a_n\\cos(nx)+b_n\\sin(nx)\n$$\n\nRecall that the corresponding Fourier coefficients of $f(-x)$ are\n\n- $a_0$ for the constant coefficient,\n- $a_n$ $n \\ge 1$, for the cosine coefficients, and\n- $-b_n$ $n \\ge 1$, for the sine coefficients.\n\nTherefore, the $5$th sine coefficient of $f(-x)$ is $-b_5$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186229676 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "532a73e6-e026-57c9-9bad-57cd2f75b6df" :knowledge-point/title "Parity Recognition and Series Type"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "947d580e-e324-5529-9683-e8139e719d3b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "odd" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186228507} {:answer/id #uuid "a6d9c53e-1e0f-5d79-bc2d-834d472fd230" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "even" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186228508}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "947d580e-e324-5529-9683-e8139e719d3b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "odd" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186228507} :answer-field/id #uuid "ce2e7bc3-7f15-5353-86d3-cb49ec8bafbf" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186228506} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a817cf48-1e5e-5542-be82-867759b96aaf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "sine terms" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186228510} {:answer/id #uuid "d02129f7-8b38-5dc9-b416-ed7585af4221" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "cosine terms" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186228511}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d02129f7-8b38-5dc9-b416-ed7585af4221" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "cosine terms" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186228511} :answer-field/id #uuid "44a32284-231f-51a0-a7ec-6a638eb11373" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186228509}] :question/id #uuid "d7903a61-d4e3-5a7b-991a-79f6efafb8b5" :question/math-academy-id "q-338682" :question/problem "Consider the function $f(x) = x\\cos (x)$ on $x ∈ [- π, π]$. Select the correct options below.\nThe function $f(x)$ is\n{{field-1}}.\n\nConsequently, the\n{{field-2}}\nin the corresponding Fourier series of $f(x)$ must be zero."}]}
